Scope and framing. All analyses are research hypotheses for MVA Hackathon 2026 Track 2 (mechanism and drug repurposing), not clinical findings or treatment recommendations. The analysis was scoped to the pharmacogenes, the {{ modsum.panel_genes if modsum else '' }}-gene mechanistic panel, genome-wide aneuploidy and genome QC described here; no screen for ACMG secondary findings was performed.

Clinical features and what may be inferred from them. The clinical features used here are the HPO terms released to hackathon participants. That set is the features made available for the challenge, not the complete clinical picture. A feature's presence in it is evidence that the feature is present in the child. A feature's absence from it is not evidence that the feature is absent: it may be absent, may not have been assessed, or may simply not have been released. Every statement in this report obeys that asymmetry. Where an inference depends on a feature being genuinely absent rather than unreported, the inference is written as conditional and says so, and no section asserts that the child lacks a feature.

Data and reference. Single-sample paired-end whole-genome sequencing from peripheral blood ({{ '{:,}'.format(qc.reads_total) if qc and qc.reads_total else 'read count not available' }} reads after alignment). Reads were re-aligned to {{ prov.reference.name }} ({{ prov.reference.build }}), rebuilt from the NCBI analysis set (md5 {{ prov.reference.source_md5 }}) with the GRC exclusion regions hard-masked and chr prefixes removed, and verified contig-by-contig (name, length, order) against the distributed VCF header. Alignment: bwa mem {{ tool('bwa') }} (-K 100000000 -Y), samtools {{ tool('samtools') }} fixmate/sort/merge and markdup (optical distance {{ params.optical_dup_distance }}). FASTQ were fetched per lane from the gated Hugging Face dataset with sha256 verification. Every CRAM-reading step passes the reference explicitly, and a first validation node compares every CRAM @SQ M5 with the reference dictionary.

Pharmacogenomics, stage 1a. The {{ forcecall.pharmcat_positions if forcecall else '(count not available)' }} PharmCAT allele-definition positions were force-called from the CRAM with bcftools mpileup/call (constrained to PharmCAT alleles, plus an unconstrained call merged in at positions carrying an undefined allele, so undocumented variation is reported rather than assumed reference; GRCh38 ploidy with the inferred sex). Constrained calling emits a genotype at every definition position by construction, so the absence of missing genotypes is a property of the method rather than evidence that the reference calls are sound; each position was therefore gated on depth >= {{ params.pgx_min_depth }} and GQ >= {{ params.pgx_min_gq }} (GQ derived from PL), with failing positions set to no-calls. PharmCAT {{ tool('pharmcat') }} (data {{ pharmcat_data_version or 'not available' }}; CPIC, DPWG and FDA sources) was run without missing-to-reference options, so a no-call reaches it as missing rather than silently becoming reference. Structural-aware star-allele calling used Aldy {{ tool('aldy') }} (profile {{ params.aldy_profile }}) on {{ params.aldy_genes.split(',') | length }} genes and, in parallel, PyPGx {{ tool('pypgx') }} (Stargazer successor; pandas pinned to {{ tool('pandas') }}). Aldy's CYP2D6 call was passed to PharmCAT as an outside call. HLA was typed from MHC-region and unmapped reads with T1K {{ tool('t1k') }} (reference IPD-IMGT/HLA {{ params.imgt_hla_version }}) and OptiType {{ tool('optitype') }}; HLA-A and HLA-B were passed to PharmCAT only when both callers agreed at 2-field resolution. Callers were reconciled per gene with explicit nomenclature normalisation and no caller preferred. MT-RNR1 (12S rRNA) was genotyped from the CRAM separately: PharmCAT's matcher does not call it, and although Aldy and PyPGx both ship definitions, Aldy addresses the mitochondrion as `MT` while this reference names it `M` (so the fetch fails), and neither caller models heteroplasmy, which is the clinically decisive quantity. It was genotyped by bcftools mpileup over {{ mt_rnr1.gene_region if mt_rnr1 else 'the gene' }} (MAPQ >= 20, base quality >= 20, depth cap 100,000), calling each of the CPIC MT-RNR1 alleles (table snapshot from the CPIC API, sha256 recorded) from allele fractions rather than a diploid genotype model: homoplasmic at AF >= {{ mt_rnr1.thresholds.homoplasmic_min if mt_rnr1 else '0.95' }}, heteroplasmic at AF >= {{ mt_rnr1.thresholds.heteroplasmic_min if mt_rnr1 else '0.05' }}; the result was passed to PharmCAT as an outside call. To show what copy-number detection changed, PharmCAT was re-run on the same VCF with every duplicated outside call collapsed to one copy, and the CPIC/DPWG annotations of the two runs were compared. Results are reported by clinical context (oncology, antiepileptic therapy, anaesthesia, supportive care); the grouping and rationale are fixed in a configuration file, and every genotype-dependent statement is PharmCAT's annotation for the called genotype. Guideline flags are counted from CPIC and DPWG only; FDA label and FDA pharmacogenetic-association text is shown with its source.

{% if ot_status in ('reported', 'example') %}Pharmacogenomics, stage 1b. Open Targets Platform ({{ db('open_targets') }}) forward (gene) and reverse (drug) pharmacogenomics annotations were joined to the child's calls; only evidence levels {{ params.ot_assert_levels }} were asserted and level-3 rows were counted as exploratory. Verdict flags come from PharmCAT's structured guideline fields (alternateDrugAvailable, dosingInformation).{% else %}Pharmacogenomics, stage 1b. The Open Targets candidate-drug join (a separate entry point, pgx_annotate.nf) was not reported for this output.{% endif %}

Modifier panel. {{ modsum.panel_genes if modsum else '(count not available)' }} genes (MVA disease genes, checkpoint-rebalance candidates, APC/C subunits, error-correction/cohesion genes; Ensembl 116 coordinates, +/-10 kb) were annotated with Ensembl VEP {{ tool('ensembl_vep') }} (offline cache {{ params.vep_cache_version }}, MANE Select), gnomAD v{{ params.gnomad_version }} joint frequencies (panel regions fetched remotely), ClinVar {{ params.clinvar_release }}, AlphaMissense and SpliceAI {{ tool('spliceai') }} run locally (masked scores, distance {{ params.spliceai_distance }}, annotation from MANE Select transcripts). Variants were flagged rare at gnomAD AF_joint < {{ params.panel_max_af }} (or absent) and functional if non-synonymous/splice or SpliceAI max delta >= {{ params.spliceai_min_delta }}; all variants, including uncertain significance, are reported. Panel-gene structural variants were called genome-wide with Delly {{ tool('delly') }} (sr), and exon copy number from mosdepth {{ tool('mosdepth') }} depth over MANE exons with exon-scale GC correction and length-aware z-scores (runs of >= 2 exons, |z| >= 3); SVs hit a gene only through overlap (DEL/DUP) or a breakpoint (INV/BND/INS), and DEL/DUP were checked against depth.

Mosaic aneuploidy. mosdepth {{ tool('mosdepth') }} depth in {{ params.bin_size }} bp bins (MAPQ >= {{ params.mosdepth_mapq }}), restricted to bins >= {{ params.aneuploidy_min_map }} uniquely mappable (Umap k100) outside the ENCODE blacklist, GC-corrected, gave LRR per bin. Heterozygous SNVs outside segmental duplications gave allele counts modelled as a beta-binomial mixture with reference bias, overdispersion and a profiled outlier fraction. For each chromosome arm, the imbalance was estimated by maximum likelihood with a profile-likelihood 95% CI and Bonferroni-corrected LRT, required to survive deletion of the 20% most imbalanced 5 Mb windows, and converted to a cell fraction under gain, loss or copy-neutral-LOH models chosen by the observed LRR. The per-arm detection limit (80% power) is reported. The model is a direct implementation validated by simulation.

Genome QC. Sex and ancestry: somalier {{ tool('somalier') }} (1000 Genomes superpopulations). Contamination: VerifyBamID2 {{ tool('verifybamid2') }} (1000 Genomes phase 3 100k hg38 SVD resource). Runs of homozygosity: bcftools roh (-G30, autosomes) with a heterozygosity-density cross-check. Coverage and mapping: mosdepth and samtools stats/flagstat, aggregated with MultiQC {{ tool('multiqc') }}.

Workflow. Nextflow DSL2 ({{ prov.pipeline.nextflow_version }}), pipeline {{ prov.pipeline.name }} {{ prov.pipeline.version }} at git commit {{ prov.pipeline.git_commit }}{% if prov.pipeline.git_dirty %} (uncommitted changes present){% endif %}; every tool version-pinned (conda environments, biocontainers or digest-pinned images); the full provenance record accompanies this report.
